msgid ""
"_An asterisk (*) after the package name indicates the package is a required "
"dependency of PyGMT._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:23
msgid "[NumPy][]*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:24
msgid ""
"The fundamental package for scientific computing in Python, providing a  "
"multidimensional array object and an assortment of routines for fast "
"operations on  arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:28
msgid "[pandas][]*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:29
msgid ""
"A Python package providing fast, flexible, and expressive data structures "
"designed to  make working with tabular data easy and intuitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:32
msgid "[xarray][]*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:33
msgid ""
"A Python package that introduces labels in the form of dimensions, "
"coordinates, and  attributes on top of raw NumPy-like arrays, which allows "
"for more intuitive, more  concise, and less error-prone user experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:37
msgid "[IPython][]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:38
msgid ""
"A rich toolkit for using Python interactively, including a powerful "
"interactive  Python shell and a Jupyter kernel to work with Python code in "
"Jupyter notebooks and  other interactive frontends. PyGMT relies on it to "
"provide a rich interactive  experience in Jupyter notebooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:43
msgid "[GeoPandas][]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:44
msgid ""
"A Python package that extends the datatypes used by [pandas][] to allow "
"spatial  operations on geometric types. PyGMT doesn't directly rely on it, "
"but supports its  two main data structures, {class}`geopandas.GeoDataFrame` "
"and  {class}`geopandas.GeoSeries`, in data processing and plotting functions/"
"methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:49
msgid "[contextily][]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:50
msgid ""
"A small Python package to retrieve tile maps from the internet. These tiles "
"can be  added as background of a map or saved to disk into geospatial raster "
"files. In PyGMT,  {func}`pygmt.datasets.load_tile_map` and {meth}`pygmt."
"Figure.tilemap` rely on it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:54
msgid "[rioxarray][]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:55
msgid ""
"A geospatial [xarray][] extension powered by [rasterio][], enabling seamless "
"reading,  writing, and manipulation of multi-dimensional arrays with "
"geospatial attributes such  as coordinate reference systems (CRS) and "
"spatial extent (bounds). PyGMT relies on it  in in several aspects:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:60
msgid ""
"To save multi-band rasters to temporary files in GeoTIFF format, to support "
"processing and plotting 3-D {class}`xarray.DataArray` images."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:62
msgid "To write CRS information to the {class}`xarray.DataArray` objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:63
msgid ""
"To reproject raster tiles to the target CRS in {func}`pygmt.datasets."
"load_tile_map`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:66
msgid ""
"We're working towards avoiding temporary files when processing/plotting "
"multi-band rasters in [PR #3468](https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/"
"pygmt/pull/3468)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:70
msgid "[PyArrow][]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:71
msgid ""
"The Python bindings for [Apache Arrow][], a development platform for in-"
"memory analytics  that specifies a standardized language-independent "
"columnar memory format for flat and  hierarchical data, organized for "
"efficient analytic operations on modern hardware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:76
msgid ""
"If you have [PyArrow][] installed, PyGMT does have some initial support for "
"`pandas.Series` and `pandas.DataFrame` objects with Apache Arrow-backed "
"arrays. Specifically, only uint/int/float, date32/date64 and string types "
"are supported for now. Support for Duration types and GeoArrow geometry "
"types is still a work in progress. For more details, see [issue #2800]"
"(https://github.com/GenericMappingTools/pygmt/issues/2800)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:84
msgid "Packages depending on PyGMT"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:86
msgid ""
"Various packages rely on PyGMT for geospatial data processing, analysis, and "
"visualization. Below is an incomplete list (in no particular order) of these "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ecosystem.md:90
msgid ""
"If your package relies on PyGMT, please [let us know](https://github.com/"
"GenericMappingTools/pygmt/issues/new) or [add it by yourself](contributing."
"md)."
msgstr ""

